## F. Methodological Note on Cross‑Model Variation

- **Persona‑driven variance** accounted for ~70% of ranking differences. Public/Caregiver weighted “visible waits/safety”; Clinicians weighted “bed‑days/flow”; Commissioner weighted “equity/value”; MT weighted “tech‑enablement/ROI”.
- **Source emphasis**: NHS England operational reports (2022–2023) dominated clinician/commissioner scores; peer‑reviewed Cochrane/CMAJ dominated vaccination and virtual‑ward confidence; MT cited more telehealth/JMIR literature.
- **Overgeneralization** observed in use of “social prescribing”, “environmental sustainability”, “neighbourhood teams” without component specification – normalised in Section A.
- **Unsupported inference**: minimal. Source texts self‑flagged uncertainties (e.g., “Morris et al. 2018 verify”, “Gordon et al. 2019 questionable”, “illustrative titles”). We retained only verifiable references.
- **Scoring权重** differed across personas (equal vs weighted); we reconciled by frequency‑of‑mention and evidence‑grade rather than composite scores.
- **Coverage gap**: LMIC feasibility inferred from intervention characteristics, not from persona data (all personas UK‑centric); we tagged income‑feasibility per Section D.

